---
description: Optical vertical centering for text buttons via descender padding (not icon buttons)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Button optical centering (descender padding)

## The bug

Flex `align-items: center` centers the **line box**, which reserves space for **descenders** (`g` `y` `p` `q`). Labels without descenders (“Plan”, “Tours”) look optically high by about that gap.

## Scope

- **Do** apply to every new text control via the shared `button` / `.button` / `a.button` / `a.secondary` base — never invent a parallel button style.
- Extend the base (override `--control-pad-*` only). Do not redefine display/padding/font/border chrome.
- **Do not** apply this padding nudge to `.icon-btn` / icon-only controls.

## Required pattern (text only)

Shrink block-end (keeps height closer to original):

```css
.button {
  --control-pad-block: 0.45rem;
  --control-descender: 0.12em;

  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  padding-block-start: var(--control-pad-block);
  padding-block-end: calc(var(--control-pad-block) - var(--control-descender));
}
```

Tune via `--control-descender` (`0.08em`–`0.16em`). No `text-box-trim` in this workspace.
